1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Canada has a couple hundred weather stations that have been running for a long, long time.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:08,500
Each one gets compared to its own normal: its average from 1961 to 1990.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:13,100
In the 1970s, 6% of them were warmer than normal.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:18,200
Then the 2000s. 263 stations. 263 were warmer.

5
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:19,600
Every single one.

6
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:25,800
From 2011 to 2020, Inuvik was 3.2 degrees above its normal.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,400
Three degrees doesn't sound like much, unless you're in Inuvik.

8
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:33,600
That decade, 216 out of the 217 were warmer.

9
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,900
The only one that wasn't was in Three Hills, Alberta.

10
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,700
I guess good for Three Hills.

